{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMopQH3BxSryffFBkgqD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the daily digest loop and wrote the report, but I only ran tests for the three packages I changed. I did not run the full `./...` suite or `make lint`. `go test` passes for `./internal/digest`, `./internal/state` and `./internal/servecmd`, and `go vet` is clean on them.\n\nThe new `digest` loop posts one comment a day on the status issue. It covers the previous complete UTC day and shows open-issue counts per `ard:` label, jobs run, failures with a per-role split, and spend. A `digest` event written after the post marks the day as done, so a restart does not repost.\n\n- **Queue depth:** it counts every `ard:` label on open non-PR issues from one list call, not the fixed label list the plan sketched.\n- **Failed post:** a failed post is logged and retried on the next tick, not returned as a tick error.\n- **Test names:** `TestRenderGolden` and `TestRestartKeepsMarker` from the plan are covered by inline-assertion tests, with no golden file.\n\nI also added the state queries the digest needs (`CountEndedSince`, `SpendBetween`) and updated the Observability bullet in `docs/proposal.md`. The README does not need a change.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/58/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":717,"cache_read_input_tokens":49909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":717},"output_tokens":417,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"034ed4df-ac22-4483-a78e-966770a69ffc","uuid":"e162ba68-075f-4e88-9530-51ae7dd61809","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:10:13.014Z","request_id":"req_011ChMopQ87BndhsqsEdwcpy"}
